      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This has happened to me recently. More than once. I didn't have logs to show at the time, but I know now there's a problem with it, as I discovered another app with the problem...\n\nI'm in Fedora on a 5700X3D / 9070 XT, using GE-Proton for VRC, but I discovered VNyan, a vtubing app, does the same thing (using Wine for VNyan, not Proton), where it's fine for a while until it suddenly isn't, and the whole system hangs on a mega I/O chokepoint. VNyan also uses the Unity engine. For me, I had to sit and wait several minutes for the system to close out the game/app for being out of memory (which I didn't know that was the problem, the system straight up froze, but I waited it out to see if the OS could recover, and it did). \n\nHaving done hardware tests (overnight memtest, etc.), I have since ruled out the problem being my PC (which has >32GB GB RAM, and when on VRC in a busy Instance rarely exceeds 16GB total RAM usage, OS and all), and I know how people feel about this, but 99% of the time a problem with a game in linux is not a linux problem. This could be a Unity engine problem, considering it's been happening with other Unity games too. I will need to test this theory by long playing more Unity games of the same Unity version.\n\nNext time this happens, I'll try and get logs too.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-04-16T16:38:46.197Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "VRChat using absurd amount of RAM, more likely on longer sessions (around 2-4 hours).\n\nI haven't played around with it too much to figure out things that could be causing it, but I have noticed that the longer the play session, the more likely it is to happen. Ends up using all of my available RAM, causing freezing and stuttering which can only be solved by restarting VRChat.\n\nDoes not reset on world/instance rejoin, or going to a new world.\n\nI have noticed that RAM usage will be stable, then at some point, it just starts to pile on more and more.\n\nONLY happens on VRChat, every other VR application and non-VR application doesn't do this.\n\nDon't know if the results are different on Desktop.\n\nThis has been happening for a while now and I first started noticing it with the release of the Lunar New Year items update. Maybe could be something that happened there?",
